@startuml
' Source block: uml251_09_communication_approximation (uml-2.5.1-legend.puml intake)
!include ../../../../tooling/styles/plantuml/interaction/communication-diagram-style.iuml
' ============================================================================
' Section 09 — Communication Diagram concepts
'
' UML traceability:
'   UML 2.5.1 §17.9 Communication Diagrams
'
' PlantUML support: Approximation.
' PlantUML's official UML diagram set does not expose a dedicated
' Communication Diagram language. This uses object/link topology
' plus manually numbered messages. It is NOT a formal replacement
' for a model-aware Communication Diagram implementation.
' ============================================================================

title UML 2.5.1 Notation Reference — Communication Diagram (Approximation)
left to right direction
skinparam monochrome true

object ":Client" as CommClient
object ":OrderService" as CommService
object ":Repository" as CommRepo
object ":PaymentGateway" as CommGateway

CommClient -- CommService : 1: submitOrder()
CommService -- CommRepo : 1.1: save()
CommService -- CommGateway : 1.2: authorize()
CommService -- CommClient : 2: confirmation()

note as CommunicationLimitations
  <b>PlantUML support: approximation</b>

  UML Communication Diagrams emphasize:
  • Lifelines/participants
  • Links among participants
  • Messages attached to links
  • Sequence expressions / numbering for ordering

  This rendering preserves topology and message numbers,
  but PlantUML does not provide a first-class UML
  Communication Diagram construct that enforces those semantics.
end note
@enduml
